# Database & Prisma

Prisma exists ONLY inside `apps/api/src/infrastructure/`. Repositories under
`persistence/prisma/` are the only database access layer — never bypass them
with ad hoc queries elsewhere.

- IDs: `@id @default(cuid())` (matches existing models — stay consistent,
  don't switch to `autoincrement()`).
- Every model has `createdAt @default(now())` and `updatedAt @updatedAt`.
- Use `@@map`/`@map` to snake_case DB names while keeping camelCase in Prisma
  Client (see existing models for the pattern).
- Add `@@index` for foreign keys and frequently filtered columns (e.g.
  `userId`, `applicationStatus`).
- Relations: always define both sides with explicit `@relation`, and choose
  `onDelete: Cascade` vs `Restrict` deliberately (Cascade for owned
  child records like rounds/questions, Restrict for shared reference data like
  `ApplicationSource`/`InterviewType`/`Skill`).
- After editing `schema.prisma`: run `pnpm db:migrate` with a descriptive
  migration name — never hand-edit an already-applied migration file.
- Never run migrations from request handlers or app startup — they are a
  release-time admin process (`prisma migrate deploy`).
